# Cloudflare Pages redirects.
#
# /i/<token> and /reset are single pages that read the rest of the URL in JS, so
# every path under them has to reach the same file with a 200 rather than a
# redirect. A 301 here would also break the association file's path matching.
#
# The target MUST be the directory (/i/), never /i/index.html. Cloudflare
# canonicalises /i/index.html back to /i/, sees the result re-match /i/*, calls
# the rule an infinite loop and REJECTS IT AT DEPLOY TIME. a5b4fdd shipped that
# way and its build log reads "Parsed 0 valid redirect rules ... Infinite loop
# detected in this rule and has been ignored" while the site served with no
# rewrites at all. After any edit here, check the deploy log says
# "Parsed 2 valid redirect rules".
/i/*      /i/      200
/reset/*  /reset/  200
